###
# Stage F8 - Task 3: Dual-Target Reviews Testing
# Tests POST /api/reviews (create review for Tour OR User)
# Tests POST /api/reviews/{id}/replies (add reply to review)
# Tests GET /api/bookings/{id}/reviews, GET /api/tours/{id}/reviews, GET /api/users/{id}/reviews
###

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5256/api

###
# 1. Login as participant1 (participant1 / pass)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "EmailOrUsername": "participant1",
  "password": "pass"
}

### Response: Copy the token
@participant1Token = ..

###
# 2. Login as participant2 (participant2 / pass)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "participant2",
  "password": "pass"
}

### Response: Copy the token
@participant2Token = <paste token here>

###
# 3. Login as organizer (organizer / pass)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "EmailOrUsername": "organizer1",
  "password": "pass"
}

### Response: Copy the token
@organizerToken = <paste token here>

###
# 4. Get participant1's bookings to find the past tour booking
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings

### Response: Copy bookingId from a completed (Paid status) booking
@bookingId = 08de494c-78f1-496b-86e6-3dd5eef0d8d3

### Also note the TourId and MotardUserId from the booking
@tourId = 08de494c-78f0-46c0-8e54-544e3f63adf5
@organizerUserId = e723975b-1110-4942-a786-cb0cd65717e6

###
# 5. GET existing reviews for this booking (should show 2 reviews we seeded)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/reviews

###
# 6. Test GET review by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/reviews/08de494d-0001-0000-0000-000000000001

###
# 7. Test GET reviews for tour
GET {{baseUrl}}/tours/{{tourId}}/reviews

###
# 8. Test GET reviews for user (organizer)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{organizerUserId}}/reviews

###
# 9. Test POST reply to review (organizer replies to their review)
# First, get a review ID from step 5 where TargetType=1 (User review of organizer)
@reviewIdForReply = 08de494d-0001-0000-0000-000000000001

POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{reviewIdForReply}}/replies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Thank you so much! It was a pleasure riding with you. Hope to see you on another tour soon!"
}

###
# 10. Test POST create new review for Tour (participant1 reviews the tour itself)
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookingId": "{{bookingId}}",
  "targetType": 0,
  "targetId": "{{tourId}}",
  "rating": 5,
  "comment": "Amazing tour route through Loire Valley! Beautiful scenery and well-organized stops."
}

###
# 11. Test duplicate review (should return 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookingId": "{{bookingId}}",
  "targetType": 1,
  "targetId": "{{organizerUserId}}",
  "rating": 4,
  "comment": "This should fail because participant1 already reviewed this motard for this booking"
}

###
# 12. Test invalid TargetId (motard not on tour - should return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookingId": "{{bookingId}}",
  "targetType": 1,
  "targetId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "rating": 5,
  "comment": "This should fail - invalid motard"
}

###
# 13. Test review for tour that hasn't started (create future booking first)
# Get future tours
GET {{baseUrl}}/tours

### Use the future tour ID (StartAt > now)
@futureTourId = 08de494c-78e1-46a9-8585-2d44da7672d6
@futureTourMotardId = 08de494c-78e8-4755-8281-e7f0a083aff8

# Create future booking
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings/request
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tourId": "{{futureTourId}}",
  "tourMotardId": "{{futureTourMotardId}}",
  "emergencyContact": "+33 6 12 34 56 78",
  "costSharingOptIn": true
}

### Get booking ID from response
@futureBookingId = d4bf4f95-31c2-48b3-93a4-9cbd6f5aa137

# Try to review future booking (should fail with 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookingId": "{{futureBookingId}}",
  "targetType": 0,
  "targetId": "{{futureTourId}}",
  "rating": 5,
  "comment": "This should fail - tour hasn't started yet"
}

###
# 14. Test reply from non-target user (should return 403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{reviewIdForReply}}/replies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "I'm not the target of this review, this should fail"
}

###
# END OF TESTS

